WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:02.755
TON 618, a quasar.

00:03.422 --> 00:10.604
TON 618 is a quasar: gas blazing as it falls into a black hole of about forty billion Suns.

00:11.141 --> 00:13.801
Its light left 10.8 billion years ago.

00:14.391 --> 00:22.304
Space has stretched since, so the map draws it where our model of the universe puts it now: about 18 billion light-years away.
